wedged follower whose next index is pinned near the beginning is consequently not repaired by the snapshot route soon after the wedge in a default configuration, and the restart path or an explicit compaction configuration (as used in the executed experiment) is what makes the repair available.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Leader state with default Config values (TrailingLogs 10240, SnapshotThreshold 8192, SnapshotInterval 120s); a follower whose replication is pinned at an early index, so the leader would have to read entries below its first stored index to serve it.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"defaultconfig-trailing-snapshot-thresholds\\\",\\\"compactlogswithtrailing-keeps-trailing-window\\\",\\\"replication-setpreviouslog-setnewlogs\\\"]}\n ]\n}\nopen('update.json','w').write(json.dumps(upd,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nprint('ok', json.load(open('update.json'))['knowledge'][0]['ref'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
